  <section>
    <templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.9" extension="2014-06-09"/>
    <code code="51847-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Evaluation + Plan note"/>
    <title>Assessment and Plan</title>
    <text><list listType="ordered"><item><content styleCode="Bold">Acute viral pharyngitis (J02.9)</content>. Sore throat with cough, runny nose, and hoarseness after colds in her household: the pattern of a viral upper respiratory infection. Modified Centor (McIsaac) score 1 (fever 1, tender nodes 1, no exudate, cough present, age over 45 minus 1). IDSA advises against testing for group A streptococcus when viral features are clear, and no antibiotic is needed. No sign of a peritonsillar abscess (no trismus, muffled voice, uvular deviation, or palatal bulge). Temperature 37.9 C. Hydration adequate, with no orthostatic drop. [S]<list><item>No streptococcal test and no antibiotic.</item><item>Acetaminophen 1 g every 6 hours as needed, no more than 3 g a day; no ibuprofen or other NSAIDs while she takes sertraline, because together they raise the risk of bleeding.</item><item>Warm drinks, honey, and saltwater gargles; at least 1.5 liters of fluid a day, with the nutrition supplement she already has.</item><item>Avoid over-the-counter cold and night-time products: most contain diphenhydramine or doxylamine, which the AGS Beers Criteria advise against at her age.</item><item>Return the same day for difficulty swallowing saliva, trouble opening her mouth, a muffled voice, breathlessness, fever above 38.5 C, or if she cannot drink; otherwise expect improvement within a week.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Major depressive disorder (F32.1)</content>. One week of sertraline 25 mg without side effects. PHQ-9 was 16 a week ago; mood unchanged today. No suicidal thoughts; the safety plan is with her. [S]<list><item>Increase sertraline to 50 mg each morning today, as planned at the last visit.</item><item>Interpersonal psychotherapy continues; her first session is next week.</item><item>988 Suicide &amp; Crisis Lifeline and the clinic number confirmed.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Partial loss of teeth with an ill-fitting partial denture (K08.409)</content>. A small denture sore that adds to her pain on swallowing and eating. [S]<list><item>Leave the denture out at night and when it hurts; dental appointment already booked for later this month.</item></list></item></list><paragraph>Guideline basis: VA/DoD Clinical Practice Guideline for the Management of Major Depressive Disorder (2022); American Geriatrics Society 2023 Updated AGS Beers Criteria for Potentially Inappropriate Medication Use in Older Adults (2023); Clinical Practice Guideline for the Diagnosis and Management of Group A Streptococcal Pharyngitis: 2012 Update by the Infectious Diseases Society of America (2012)</paragraph><paragraph>Follow-up: Depression review in three weeks as planned; sooner, or the same day, for the warning signs above. Next scheduled visit 1603-02-23: four-week depression treatment review with a sodium check. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
